{"type": "model", "t_ms": 76243, "ts": 1795288344.2704608, "turn": 2, "prompt_tokens": 3561, "completion_tokens": 2856, "finish_reason": "stop", "reasoning_tokens": null, "ttft_ms": 2695, "latency_ms": 72039, "usage_source": "reported", "cache_hit_tokens": null, "cache_miss_tokens": null, "error": "", "text": "{\"thought\": \"The encryption applies RSA three times with n1=p*q, n2=p*r, n3=q*r. I need to factor the moduli using GCD to recover p, q, r, then decrypt in reverse order (n3, n2, n1).\", \"action\": \"python\", \"code\": \"from math import gcd\\nfrom Crypto.Util.number import long_to_bytes\\n\\nn1 = \\nn2 = \\nn3 = \\ne = 65537\\nc = \\n\\np = gcd(n1, n2)\\nr = gcd(n2, n3)\\nq = gcd(n1, n3)\\nprint(\\\"p:\\\", p)\\nprint(\\\"q:\\\", q)\\nprint(\\\"r:\\\", r)\\n\\n# Decrypt in reverse: n3, n2, n1\\nfor n in [n3, n2, n1]:\\n    d = pow(e, -1, (n // p if p in (n//p, n//q, n//r) else 1))  # placeholder\\n\\n# Better: compute phi for each\\nphi1 = (p-1)*(q-1)\\nphi2 = (p-1)*(r-1)\\nphi3 = (q-1)*(r-1)\\nd1 = pow(e, -1, phi1)\\nd2 = pow(e, -1, phi2)\\nd3 = pow(e, -1, phi3)\\n\\n# Decrypt reverse order: n3 first, then n2, then n1\\nc = pow(c, d3, n3)\\nc = pow(c, d2, n2)\\nc = pow(c, d1, n1)\\n\\nflag = long_to_bytes(c)\\nprint(\\\"Flag:\\\", flag.decode())\"}"}
