{"type": "model", "t_ms": 97756, "ts": 1795288365.7829928, "turn": 4, "prompt_tokens": 6815, "completion_tokens": 374, "finish_reason": "stop", "reasoning_tokens": null, "ttft_ms": 487, "latency_ms": 10658, "usage_source": "reported", "cache_hit_tokens": null, "cache_miss_tokens": null, "error": "", "text": "{\"thought\": \"The decryption order is wrong. The encryption applies n1 first, then n2, then n3. So decryption must be reverse: n3, n2, n1. But I need to check which primes go with which modulus. n1=p*q, n2=p*r, n3=q*r. Let me fix the decryption order and handle the bytes properly.\", \"action\": \"run_script\", \"script\": \"from math import gcd\\nfrom Crypto.Util.number import long_to_bytes\\n\\nwith open('./challenge/public-key.txt') as f:\\n    lines = f.read().strip().split('\\\\n')\\n\\nvals = {}\\nfor line in lines:\\n    k, v = line.split(': ')\\n    vals[k] = int(v)\\n\\nn1, n2, n3, e, c = vals['n1'], vals['n2'], vals['n3'], vals['e'], vals['c']\\n\\np = gcd(n1, n2)\\nq = gcd(n1, n3)\\nr = n1 // p\\n\\ndef decrypt(c, n, p, q):\\n    phi = (p-1)*(q-1)\\n    d = pow(e, -1, phi)\\n    return pow(c, d, n)\\n\\n# Encryption: c = pow(pow(pow(m, e, n1), e, n2), e, n3)\\n# Decryption: reverse order: n3, n2, n1\\nc = decrypt(c, n3, q, r)\\nc = decrypt(c, n2, p, r)\\nc = decrypt(c, n1, p, q)\\n\\nflag = long_to_bytes(c)\\nprint(flag.decode('latin-1'))\"}"}
