{"type": "model", "t_ms": 180958, "ts": 1795288448.98451, "turn": 5, "prompt_tokens": 7535, "completion_tokens": 2959, "finish_reason": "stop", "reasoning_tokens": null, "ttft_ms": 451, "latency_ms": 82131, "usage_source": "reported", "cache_hit_tokens": null, "cache_miss_tokens": null, "error": "", "text": "{\"thought\": \"The decryption order is wrong. Let me try different orders. The encryption is: c = pow(pow(pow(m, e, n1), e, n2), e, n3). So decryption should be: m = decrypt(decrypt(decrypt(c, n3), n2), n1). But I need to make sure I'm using the right primes for each modulus. n1=p*q, n2=p*r, n3=q*r. Let me try all permutations.\", \"action\": \"python\", \"code\": \"from math import gcd\\nfrom Crypto.Util.number import long_to_bytes\\n\\nn1 = \\nn2 = \\nn3 = \\ne = 65537\\nc = \\n\\np = gcd(n1, n2)\\nq = gcd(n1, n3)\\nr = n1 // p\\n\\nprint(f\\\"p = {p}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"q = {q}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"r = {r}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"n1 = p*q: {p*q == n1}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"n2 = p*r: {p*r == n2}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"n3 = q*r: {q*r == n3}\\\")\\n\\ndef decrypt(c, n, p, q):\\n    phi = (p-1)*(q-1)\\n    d = pow(e, -1, phi)\\n    return pow(c, d, n)\\n\\n# Try all 6 permutations of decryption order\\nfrom itertools import permutations\\n\\nmoduli = [('n1', n1, p, q), ('n2', n2, p, r), ('n3', n3, q, r)]\\n\\nfor perm in permutations(moduli):\\n    try:\\n        c1 = c\\n        for name, n, pp, qq in perm:\\n            c1 = decrypt(c1, n, pp, qq)\\n        result = long_to_bytes(c1)\\n        if b'picoCTF' in result:\\n            print(f\\\"SUCCESS with order: {[x[0] for x in perm]}\\\")\\n            print(f\\\"Flag: {result.decode()}\\\")\\n    except Exception as ex:\\n        pass\"}"}
